course: dictionary
lesson: 1048
title: Borrower: who borrows and pays back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A borrower is a person who borrows something. In a library, a borrower takes out a book and brings it back later. Library borrowers have library cards to do this.
explain: With money, a borrower is a person or business that borrows money from a bank and must pay it back, often with extra called interest. «Banks lend saved money to people and businesses and charge them interest; borrowers pay more interest than savers get.» So the borrower pays back more than they borrowed.
explain: Look at the word parts: borrow plus -er. The -er ending turns a word into the person who does the action, like a teacher teaches. So a borrower is someone who borrows, whether it is a book or money.
fact: A borrower is a person who borrows something, such as a book from a library.
fact: A borrower who borrows money must pay it back, often with interest.
fact: «Subprime borrower» means a borrower with a bad credit history: a record of not paying back borrowed money on time.
fact: «Creditworthy» means likely to pay back; banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy by looking at income and past borrowing.
fact: In the story The Borrowers, the borrowers are tiny people who borrow things from humans.
exercise: Sam takes three books out of the school library. What is Sam? | A lender | *A borrower | A banker | A saver
exercise: «Borrowers pay more interest than savers get.» Who pays the extra interest? | The bank's cleaner | The saver | *The borrower | The librarian
exercise: «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy.» What does creditworthy mean? | Full of library books | Very rich | Able to lend money to others | *Likely to pay back
test: In «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy», what does creditworthy mean? | *Likely to pay back the money they owe | Able to borrow no money | Good at reading | Likely to pay back
test: What is a subprime borrower? | A library card holder | *A borrower with a bad credit history | A saver with lots of interest
exam: Which person is a borrower? | A teacher who hands out books in class | *A child who takes a book home from the library | A shop assistant who sells books | A bus driver
